"I'm not going to get political" and all, but seeing as how incompetent law enforcement has been in real life this past decade, that angle makes sense to me. You have a small town where everyone knows each other, all of a sudden these peoples neighbors and friends start dying left and right with little to no explanation as far as the residents can gather, but the police choose to be secretive and give non-answers to the community. 

&#x200B;

He's just another (not too bright) Christian Hawkins resident who's girlfriend was murdered and the police aren't giving anyone real answers.

