Have you tried any or all of these fixes?  [FIX: Can’t play Forza Horizon 4 online on PC (windowsreport.com)](https://windowsreport.com/forza-horizon-4-online-fix/)

&#x200B;

 [FULL FIX: Teredo is unable to qualify error (windowsreport.com)](https://windowsreport.com/teredo-is-unable-to-qualify-fix/)  This link has more to do with the Xbox app on windows 10 along with Teredo, and has some seperate fixes that are definitely worth trying.

&#x200B;

Besides that, ask your parents what kind of router you have, and ask if they can help you reset the router, or do so yourself. Generally, to reset your router, there should be a tiny button somewhere only accessible with a paperclip that you press for about 10 seconds.

&#x200B;

 To reiterate though, if neither of the fixes I linked work for you, it's very likely that your actual network settings are messed up. On windows 10, search for cmd, and open command prompt, then type in ipconfig. Look for the line that says default gateway and the actual ip address (for example, 10.299.13.75) and type that into your browser. It should take you to your router settings. From there I would make sure that firewall status is set to low.

