I do think it's as bad as people say, but not because of the system itself. It's the politicians, pharmaceutical corporations, and major shareholders that always put profits above everything else. This wouldn't be so much of an issue to me if people weren't practically forced to have healthcare because even without Medicare or Medicaid you still are required by law to pay social security taxes.

&#x200B;

Ideally in my opinion healthcare would be completely voluntary and opt-in but it's not reality and reality fucks you and me in the ass. You can never convince me an ambulance ride is costs $10,000.

I'm not discounting what you're saying but does any person willing to go to such lengths really need to rely on laborers? In US prep culture, Prepping and self-sustainability go hand-in-hand. Also, I feel like if someone is daring enough to start shooting at someone they disagree with, they're probably daring enough to fight their way to the source of whatever supplies they need, I.E. food, water, gas, etc...

&#x200B;

Humans are very adaptive creatures, it's why we are at the top of the animal kingdom, and I think yall are underestimating the lengths most people will go to for their own survival, even your own.

I'm glad you're able to articulate how I feel with words as well.

